WEBVTT

00:00:12.773 --> 00:00:14.788
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Can you play a musical instrument?

00:00:15.339 --> 00:00:16.000
<v><b>Duncan:</b></v> I can.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.865
I can play the violin.

00:00:18.392 --> 00:00:19.920
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How well do you play it?

00:00:20.573 --> 00:00:21.368
<v><b>Duncan:</b></v> Not very.

00:00:26.914 --> 00:00:28.738
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you have noisy neighbors?

00:00:29.278 --> 00:00:31.001
<v><b>Alice:</b></v> Yes, I have noisy neighbors.

00:00:31.025 --> 00:00:32.087
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do they do?

00:00:33.182 --> 00:00:34.955
<v><b>Alice:</b></v> My neighbors like to have parties.

00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:37.997
Every day and every night.

00:00:44.438 --> 00:00:46.514
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What’s your favorite month of the year?

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:47.997
Why?

00:00:48.626 --> 00:00:53.062
<v><b>Tiffany:</b></v> My favorite month is December because it gets colder,

00:00:53.879 --> 00:00:56.014
and I like snow and cold weather.

00:00:56.931 --> 00:00:58.157
And I like Christmas time.

00:01:03.921 --> 00:01:05.598
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What kind of music do you like?

00:01:07.042 --> 00:01:08.366
<v><b>Stephen:</b></v> A lot of kinds of music.

00:01:08.599 --> 00:01:14.334
Um, I typically listen to electronic dance, and um, indie rock.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:19.939
I listen to the new folk, they call it. But I like opera and a lot of jazz.

00:01:20.485 --> 00:01:21.533
The list could go on.

00:01:21.755 --> 00:01:23.744
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What kind of music don’t you like?

00:01:24.672 --> 00:01:25.985
<v><b>Stephen:</b></v> I don’t like country music.

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:28.638
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you have a favorite band or singer?

00:01:29.039 --> 00:01:30.085
<v><b>Stephen:</b></v> Sure.

00:01:30.292 --> 00:01:35.265
Right now, my favorite band is Wye Oak from Brooklyn.

00:01:41.348 --> 00:01:42.958
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What kind of books do you like?

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:49.964
<v><b>Dasha:</b></v> Um, I read like all sorts of books, from history books to like, novels,

00:01:49.989 --> 00:01:54.186
and all sorts of books, really.

00:01:54.366 --> 00:01:56.007
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What are you reading at the moment?

00:01:56.007 --> 00:01:59.254
<v><b>Dasha:</b></v> Uh, at the moment, I’m reading a history of modern France.